{"name":"Black Queen","hex":"#694d27","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"queen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The wife, consort, or widow of a king.","A female monarch."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act the part of a queen; to behave imperiously; to queen it.","To make a queen or (figuratively) to give the status of a queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Queen, Lightning Ridge","blocks":[{"text":"The Black Queen is a house made of 14,000 glass bottles located in Lightning Ridge in outback NSW, Australia, and a theatre show of the same name at the same location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/The_Black_Queen%2C_Lightning_Ridge%2C_NSW.jpg/330px-The_Black_Queen%2C_Lightning_Ridge%2C_NSW.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Queen%2C_Lightning_Ridge"},{"title":"Michael Morpurgo","blocks":[{"text":"Sir Michael Andrew Bridge Morpurgo is an English book author, poet, playwright, and librettist who is known best for children's novels such as War Horse (1982). His work is noted for its \"magical storytelling\", for recurring themes such as the triumph of an outsider or survival, for characters' relationships with nature, and for vivid settings such as the Cornish coast or the trenches of the First World War. Morpurgo was the third Children's Laureate, from 2003 to 2005, and is President of BookTrust, a children's reading charity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Michael_Morpurgo_20090315_Salon_du_livre_1.jpg/330px-Michael_Morpurgo_20090315_Salon_du_livre_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Morpurgo"},{"title":"Black Queen (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Queen, in comics, may refer to:"},{"items":["Marvel Comics characters, members of Hellfire Club:\nSelene (comics), replaced Phoenix after the Dark Phoenix Saga\nEmma Steed, part of the London branch's Inner Circle\nEmma Frost, the former White Queen used the alias when she was part of the Dark X-Men","Selene (comics), replaced Phoenix after the Dark Phoenix Saga","Emma Steed, part of the London branch's Inner Circle","Emma Frost, the former White Queen used the alias when she was part of the Dark X-Men","DC Comics characters, who are members of Checkmate:\nPatricia Grace-Colby, during the events around The OMAC Project\nSasha Bordeaux, in the post-Infinite Crisis line-up","Patricia Grace-Colby, during the events around The OMAC Project","Sasha Bordeaux, in the post-Infinite Crisis line-up"]},{"items":["Selene (comics), replaced Phoenix after the Dark Phoenix Saga","Emma Steed, part of the London branch's Inner Circle","Emma Frost, the former White Queen used the alias when she was part of the Dark X-Men"]},{"items":["Patricia Grace-Colby, during the events around The OMAC Project","Sasha Bordeaux, in the post-Infinite Crisis line-up"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Queen_(comics)"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg/500px-Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg/500px-Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Queen_Victoria_after_Heinrich_von_Angeli.jpg/500px-Queen_Victoria_after_Heinrich_von_Angeli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Queen_Victoria_after_Heinrich_von_Angeli.jpg/500px-Queen_Victoria_after_Heinrich_von_Angeli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQueen_Victoria_by_Heinrich_von_Angeli.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg/500px-Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg/500px-Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada